# Fight silhouette (D-048)

Live fight cutouts only (`practice_fight` / Mythmir / `pvp_fight` / yard wire):

| `data-role` | Visual mass |
|---|---|
| assassin / mage | floor (smallest; still bumped vs pre-D-048) |
| ranger | slight above floor |
| support | mid |
| fighter | large |
| tank | largest |

- Size via art-well `--mf-role-h` / `--mf-role-w` (height/width), **not** `transform` on the sprite — tall assassin art must not out-head a tank.
- Vars on `.mf-battle-unit--cutout` from `decorateBattleUnitIdle` → `data-role`.
- Flip stays `scaleX(-1)` on `.mf-sprite-face` only (idle breathe owns img `transform`).
- Monsters use the **same** role map as cats.
- Practice dummies (`[data-dummy]`): **one** size ≈ fighter + `--mf-dummy-zoom` on `.mf-sprite-face` (PNG fringe); flip composes `scaleX(-1) scale(zoom)`.
- Practice: one art-well formula for allies and enemies under cutout mode (no enemy-only `aspect-[2/3]` taller well).
- Do **not** role-size lobby / background portraits (`D-037`).
- Do not shrink roles below the assassin floor — bump tank/fighter up instead.
